            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures+in+model+theory"} mathematical structures
          %p
            A model theory for a particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            typically works within a given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe"} universe
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} mathematical structure
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+in+model+theory"} structure for a language
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definition"} definition
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth"} truth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} language
            (function symbols, relations symbols and constants), and formulas (formed from symbols,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantifiers"} quantifiers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+variables"} free variables
            (viewed as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axioms"} axioms
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            via a given set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            together with interpretation of the symbols of the language. A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
            in the language
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+in+model+theory"} L-structure
            which satisfies each formula in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
          %p The two main problems of model theory are
          %ul
            %li
              classification of a given theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{T}
              in a language
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %li
              study the family of all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+sets"} definable sets
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+%28in+model+theory%29"} structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/language+%28in+model+theory%29"} language
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %p
            In all memorable examples, the collection of structures for a language will form an interesting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (see
            %a{:href => "#BekeRosicky11"} Beke-Rosicky 11
            for a characterization of these), and the subcollection of those structures verifying a given collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Th
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Th
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            in the language are an interesting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
            again.
          %p
            Model theory as currently conceived has strong analogies with the classical theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+varieties"} algebraic varieties
            and hence with the part of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            that deals with these. One such analogy is that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definable+subsets"} definable subsets
            are likened to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+loci"} zero loci
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations"} equations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            which can be likened to Krull dimension. One can also say that classical algebraic geometry often provides a testing ground for more general developments in model theory. (For the most part, model theory does not deal however with more global concepts of modern algebraic geometry such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            or
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
          %h2#Scope Scope
          %p
            In full generality,
            %em model theory
            would study all kinds of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            over all kinds of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
          %p
            Traditionally the default subject of model theory (e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Hodges93"}> Hodges 93
            )) are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theories"} first-order theories
            (only) and their models in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            (only), these are the traditional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures+in+model+theory"} structures in model theory
            %em first-order model theory
            or
            %em classical model theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#SEPEntry"}> SEP
            ). Among the fundamental classfication theorems provable in this context are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compactness+theorem"} compactness theorem
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L%C3%B6wenheim-Skolem+theorem"} Löwenheim-Skolem theorem
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stability+theory"} geometric stability theory
          %p
            More modern developments in model theory consider also wider classes of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            than just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theories"} first-order theories
            (e.g
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#TentZiegler12"} Tent-Ziegler 12
            %a{:href => "#CategoricalModelTheory"} categorical model theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#MakkaiPare89"}> Makkai-Paré 89
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BekeRosicky11"} Beke-Rosicky 11
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            Classical model theory is concerned with models of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theories"} theories
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+logic"} first-order logic
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#FirstOrderLogic"}> First-order logic
              \.
          %p
            More generally one can consider models over theories in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher-order+logic"} higher-order logic
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#HigherOrderLogic"}> Higher-order logic
              \.
          %h3#FirstOrderLogic Classical Model theory in First-order logic
          %p
            See also/first
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
          .standout
            %p
              %strong Caveat Lector.
              This may duplicate/contradict other nLab accounts of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FOL"} FOL
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
              %em addressing
              rather than
              %em naming
              of variables; specifically, the variable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_n
              occurs
              %em bound
              in a formula if it is nested within more than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              quantifiers, and otherwise
              = succeed "." do
                %em free
          %p
            We describe an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            over two
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            for “words” and “propositions”, respectively. The full operad is freely generated by various disjoint suboperads
          %ul
            %li
              a free suboperad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
              of operations, or functions, of types
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^n\to W
            %li
              an
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of variables of types
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to W
            %li
              a (free) suboperad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              of predicates, or relations, of types
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^n\to P
            %li
              the equality operad, of type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mn 2
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^2\to P
            %li
              the boolean operad,
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge, \vee,\neg,\dots
              of types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi P
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^{k}\to P
              for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=1,2
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=0
              if you want to include
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊥
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            %li
              the quantifier
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %mo :
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall:
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall x_j
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi j
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_j\in X_0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P\to P
          %p
            Notable subsets of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            include
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O[X]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo ∪
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O\cup X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[X]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ?
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ? \to P
            in the suboperad generated by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo ,
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O,R,X
          %p
            Abusively, an
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                \-structure
            %em interpretation
            of the functions and relations is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+operad"} algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi O
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (W,P,O,R)\mapsto (M,2,O_M,R_M)
            for the suboperad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            generated by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                  %mo ∪
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O\cup R
            with the type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            interpreted by the initial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+algebra"} boolean algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            The
            %em Tarski Definition of Truth
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} natural
            extension of the
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            to an
            = succeed "-algebra," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M,\dots)
            such that * for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[X]
            and for all functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:X\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi[m]
            is true in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi Θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi \wedge \Theta
            is true if for all functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m:X\to M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi[m]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Θ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Theta[m]
            are true, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg \Phi
            is true if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em not
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∀
                  %mo :
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\forall:\Phi)[m]
            is true in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            precisely when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi[m_a]
            is true for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in M
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo =
                            %mn 0
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi x
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi else
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_a(x_i) = \left\{ \array{ a &amp; i=0 \\ m(x_{i-1}) &amp; else }\right.
          %p (Again, this really should be written more clearly, but it’s a start.)
          .query
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/JCMcKeown"}> JCMcKeown
              \: is there some nicer way to say the quantifier nonsense? I’m thinking along the lines
            %blockquote
              %p
                there are two actions of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
                on
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∀
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall
                quantifier; and the Tarski extension is the one that makes these commute somehow
            %p
              %em> ibid
              \: maybe it’s more right to say that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi P
                      %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P_M
              should be the boolean algebra
              = succeed "?" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi M
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(|M|^\mathbb{N})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              on it…
          %h4#definition_theory_and_model_fol Definition and remarks
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-structure" do
